Ekwang Recipe

Ingredients:

2kg cocoyams

500g cocoyam leaves or taro leaves

500g beef

250g cow skin

200g smoked fish

1 cup ground crayfish

1 cup red palm oil

2 seasoning cubes

Fresh pepper to taste

Salt to taste

Water as needed

Preparation:

Peel the cocoyams and wash them thoroughly. Grate them into a smooth paste.

Wash the cocoyam leaves and cut them into suitable pieces.

Place a small amount of grated cocoyam onto each leaf and roll it carefully to form small wraps.

Arrange the wraps tightly in a pot lined with cocoyam leaves, placing them close together so they do not open during cooking.

Wash the beef and cow skin. Season with salt and cook until tender. Add the smoked fish and set aside.

Pour the red palm oil over the wrapped cocoyam leaves. Add the ground crayfish, pepper, seasoning cubes, and a little water.

Cover the pot and cook over low to medium heat for about 1½ to 2 hours. Avoid stirring vigorously so the wraps remain intact.

Add the cooked meat, cow skin, and smoked fish. Continue cooking until the cocoyam paste is fully cooked and the sauce is thick and well combined.

Taste and adjust the salt and seasoning. Add a little hot water if necessary.

Serve hot and enjoy your traditional Cameroonian Ekwang.
